        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Whitefield, Charles Wesley, Edward Perronet\n- Organizations: Trefeca College, Church of England, St Peter's parish at Eastern Hill\n- Topics: 18th-century religious movement, priest collaborator\n\nFacts:\n- In the 18th century, the Trefeca College movement began within the Church of England.\n- George Whitefield and Charles Wesley were among the people who started the Trefeca College movement.\n- A priest who worked with Edward Perronet also helped start the Trefeca College movement.\n- The priest who worked with Edward Perronet was of the same denomination as St Peter's parish at Eastern Hill.",
